      <div type="clause" n="19">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:QuadrDed">Quadr Ded</ref> 19</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Quadr Ded 19" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="530" ed="#liebermann"/>Nulla diuinæ miserationis opera, nulla malorum flagella respiciunt. Ubi sunt qui dicuntur de supremo singulorum exitu iudicare? Uidemus bonorum duros exitus, nocentum felices. Ubi sunt qui dicebant, peccata mundi per dies singulos [d]iis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#QuadrDed_19.lnote.oe.11"/> ultricibus nunciari? Humano sumus et diuino iuditio propemodum destituti; pene<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="l" target="#QuadrDed_19.lnote.oe.l"/> effusi sunt gressus mei!</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 530 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="QuadrDed_19.lnote.oe.l" n="l" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">530</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Psalm</hi> 72, 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Psalm</hi> 72, 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="QuadrDed_19.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">530</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">oder</hi> Diris <hi rend="italic">i. e.</hi> Furiis; aíis <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">or</hi> Diris <hi rend="italic">i. e.</hi> Furiis; aíis <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg></note>
      </div>
